.TH geectl-branch-copy-package 1  "geectl-branch-copy-package 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-branch\-copy\-package \- Copy a package to another project (or another OBS instance with `\-\-to\-apiurl`). A mutation: dry\-run is the default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl branch copy\-package\fR [\fB\-\-revision\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-link\fR] [\fB\-\-expand\fR] [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-\-noservice\fR] [\fB\-\-dont\-update\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-vrev\fR] [\fB\-\-to\-apiurl\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-source\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-source\-package\fR> <\fB\-\-target\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-target\-package\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy a package to another project (or another OBS instance with `\-\-to\-apiurl`). A mutation: dry\-run is the default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-project\fR \fI<SOURCE_PROJECT>\fR
The project to copy from
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-package\fR \fI<SOURCE_PACKAGE>\fR
The package to copy
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The project to copy to
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The package to copy to
.TP
\fB\-\-revision\fR \fI<REVISION>\fR
Copy this source revision instead of the latest
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-link\fR
Keep the source package\*(Aqs link when copying a link package
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\fR
Copy the expanded source (the link resolved) instead of the link itself
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR
A comment recorded on the copy
.TP
\fB\-\-noservice\fR
Do not run source services on the copied files
.TP
\fB\-\-dont\-update\-source\fR
Do not update the source package when copying a link onto its target
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-vrev\fR
Carry the source revision\*(Aqs vrev over to the copy
.TP
\fB\-\-to\-apiurl\fR \fI<TO_APIURL>\fR
Copy to another OBS instance at this API URL instead of the configured one. The target\*(Aqs credentials come from the instance alias matching that URL in the config file\*(Aqs `[instances]` table (`GEECTL_OBS_APIKEY[_FILE]_<ALIAS>` or `GEECTL_OBS_USERNAME_<ALIAS>` / `GEECTL_OBS_PASSWORD[_FILE]_<ALIAS>`; see `auth::resolve_obs_for_url`) and the copy fails clearly when none are configured — the source instance\*(Aqs credentials are never forwarded to the target. The copy is client\-side and always expanded; `\-\-keep\-link` and the server\-side copy options are refused with it
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
